menu "Status LED"
    config ESP_STATUS_LED_ENABLED
        bool "Enable RGB LED status indicator"
        default n
        help 
            If enabled, a WS2812B (NeoPixel) LED will be used to visually indicate the current status of the ESP32 (e.g., Wi-Fi connecting, connected, errors).

    if ESP_STATUS_LED_ENABLED
        config ESP_STATUS_LED_GPIO
            int "The GPIO pin of the LED"
            default 48
            help
                The GPIO pin connected to the addressable RGB LED.
                Default is 48, which is the built-in NeoPixel on the ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1.

        config ESP_STATUS_LED_BRIGHTNESS
            int "LED Brightness (1-100)"
            range 1 100
            default 20
            help
                Sets the maximum brightness of the status LED as a percentage.
                Addressable LEDs are extremely bright at 100%. A value between 10 and 20 is highly recommended for indoor use.

        config ESP_STATUS_LED_UART_ACTIVITY
            bool "Flash LED on UART Data Activity"
            default y
            help
                If enabled, the LED will flash rapidly when data is sent or received over UART.
                Disable this if you find the constant flashing during high data transfer distracting.
    endif
endmenu
